            "type": "text",
            "text": "Here's a model where you set the drip flow and watch the 6-minute bucket total.\n\n```openui lifecycle=ephemeral id=drip-irrigation-sim\n\nroot = LearningSurface([sim], \"Drip irrigation: flow to bucket\", \"Set the drip flow rate and read the 6-minute bucket total.\", \"ephemeral\")\nsim = Simulation(\"drip-sim\", \"Flow to bucket over 6 minutes\", [\n  { id: \"flow\", label: \"Drip flow rate\", unit: \"L/min\", min: 0.5, max: 20, step: 0.5, value: 2 }\n], [\n  { id: \"bucket\", label: \"Water in bucket\", unit: \"L\", expr: \"flow * 6\", precision: 1, emphasis: true },\n  { id: \"rate\", label: \"Flow rate\", unit: \"L/min\", expr: \"flow\", precision: 1 }\n], \"ephemeral\", \"Move the flow slider. The bucket line reads flow × 6 minutes, assuming no losses to evaporation or runoff. Press Share what I found to send your settings back.\")\n```\n\nDrag the slider and watch the bucket total scale linearly — every 0.5 L/min adds 3 L over the 6 minutes."
          }
        ]
      },
